assistant: Subject: retry get_order briefly when a new order 404s

The v2 vendor (2026-10-01) is eventually consistent: `POST /orders` returns the new order (`o-5002`), but an immediate `GET /orders/o-5002` can still return 404, and `get_order` reported that as "No order with id". This is my best inference, not something I confirmed: the spec is unchanged, the ids match, and the repo has no other hint. The fix is in `src/tools/get_order.ts`. When the vendor returns 404, it now asks again up to 3 times, waiting 100/200/300 ms, and only reports "not found" if the order still isn't there. A real 200 is returned unchanged. The v1 fixtures never 404, so they make the same requests and give the same output. Typecheck and lint pass and the v1 contract suite stays green, but the repro test is still red. The extra GET isn't in the recording, so the test fails with UNMATCHED_REQUEST until it's re-recorded with `fiks rerecord`, which I couldn't run here. That re-record will also test whether the retry is enough: the recorded 404 had no Retry-After header. Its `created_at` comes back as epoch milliseconds, which the current parsing turns into 1970, so it may flag other v2 changes too.

